  "description": "UQAWES crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H49 Br4 N8 O29 Pr4 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Pr01 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr02 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr03 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr04 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.789-5.356 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.62-164.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C70H63Br4N9O30Pr4.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
